---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import PageHeader from '../components/PageHeader.astro';
import { site, url } from '../data/site';
---

<Base
  title="About"
  description={`FinvestLens is published by ${site.publisher.legalName}. A native Apple accounting app, free software under the GPL v3.`}
>
  <PageHeader eyebrow="About" title="About FinvestLens" lead="Why it exists, who publishes it, and the terms it comes under." />

  <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-5 py-16">
    <div class="prose-doc">
      <h2>Why it exists</h2>
      <p>
        GnuCash is a mature, trusted, free-software accounting package built on
        rigorous double-entry bookkeeping. Its desktop interface, though, is GTK:
        it does not look or behave like a Mac app, there is no iPad or iPhone
        version, and none of the Apple platform conveniences are there.
      </p>
      <p>
        FinvestLens exists to give people in the Apple ecosystem a first-class
        native accounting app that keeps the correctness of GnuCash’s engine, feels
        genuinely at home on the platform, runs on macOS, iPadOS and iOS from one
        codebase, and stays interoperable so nobody is locked in.
      </p>
      <p>
        It is <strong>not</strong> a fork of GnuCash. It is a clean, idiomatic Swift
        reimplementation of GnuCash’s concepts and data model, designed for Apple
        platforms from the ground up. Correctness is checked by importing a real
        46,000-transaction GnuCash book and comparing every balance, report and
        register against GnuCash itself.
      </p>

      <h2 id="publisher">Published by Hello Tham</h2>
      <p>
        FinvestLens is published by
        <a href={site.publisher.url}>{site.publisher.legalName}</a>, a boutique
        management consulting firm whose work is summed up in its own words as
        “{site.publisher.tagline}”: <em>“We help organisations around the world
        define and implement their vision and objectives.”</em>
      </p>
      <p>
        The firm specialises in business and IT strategies, operating models,
        strategic roadmaps, enterprise architecture, analytics and business process
        design. Releases of FinvestLens are signed and notarized under its Apple
        Developer identity.
      </p>
      <p>
        More at <a href={site.publisher.url}>hellotham.com</a>.
      </p>

      <h2 id="licence">Licence</h2>
      <p>
        FinvestLens is free software, distributed under the
        <strong>GNU General Public License v3.0</strong> — the same copyleft family
        GnuCash uses. That keeps FinvestLens licence-compatible with GnuCash, so its
        concepts and, where useful, its source can be drawn on directly.
      </p>
      <p>
        The complete source is at <a href={site.repo}>github.com/hellotham/finvestlens</a>.
        You may use, study, share and modify it under the terms of the licence.
      </p>

      <h2>A note on GnuCash</h2>
      <p>
        The GnuCash XML format is treated here as an interchange specification.
        FinvestLens is not an official GnuCash product, and is not affiliated with
        or endorsed by the GnuCash project. Our thanks to them all the same — the
        model this app rests on is theirs.
      </p>

      <h2>Not financial advice</h2>
      <p>
        FinvestLens records and reports on your own figures. Its planners, tax
        estimator and wellbeing score are estimates computed from your data and your
        assumptions, always shown with their workings. They are not financial, tax
        or investment advice, and no part of the app should be treated as such.
      </p>

      <h2>Get in touch</h2>
      <p>
        Questions, bugs and feature requests are welcome — see
        <a href={url('/support/')}>support</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
